      <div class="prose">
        <p>My name is Truong and I'm proud to be Vietnamese — the food alone is worth it. 🍜</p>
        <p>I graduated with a Computer Science degree from San Francisco State University in 2013, then spent 2014–2019 in Vietnam working at Ogilvy Vietnam as a front-end engineer for 5+ years. After moving back to the US, I freelanced for a while.</p>
        <p>Before landing at Costco, I was managing a sandwich store from A to Z — daily operations, the team, the customers, everything. Since June, I've been with the Costco team, bringing that same work ethic to a new environment. I still love building for the web and tinker with side projects whenever I can.</p>
        <p>I write about code, travel, photography, and life here — in English and Vietnamese.</p>
        <p>For the professional stuff, head to my <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/truong-nguyen-dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn profile</a>. And <a href="/contact/">say hi</a> if you want to chat. 😄</p>
        <p>Or sneak a peek at my <a href="https://truongnguyen.notion.site/e5fb5ef2f8294b1a939d617c1c20e946?v=98b521f37ac04beea42db4fc4276cce3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Keyboard Showroom</a> ⌨️</p>
      </div>
    </div>
